cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or retained evidence, cite the accompanying manuscript."
title: "In-Context Collapse in Vision-Language Models and How to Mitigate It"
abstract: >-
  Controlled studies of in-context performance degradation and selective adapter
  recovery in vision-language models. The revised evidence distinguishes source
  classification recovery, limited target transfer, mechanism-consistent controls,
  and negative rule-selection and image-disjoint VQA repair tests. Historical
  breadth results retain their stated aggregate and heterogeneous-protocol limits.
authors:
